<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- harbor:template-only
     THIS FILE IS A TEMPLATE (harbor#630). Do not cp it: @HOME@ and the other placeholders in it would be
     installed as literal text, and launchd loads such a job and then fails every time it runs. Render it:

       sh ~/port/harbor/bin/deploy-launchd-render.sh ~/port/harbor/launchd/com.harbor.findings.plist > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.harbor.findings.plist

     A cp line in the comment below predates the template. It is kept so the rendered file stays byte-identical
     to the one already installed: follow this block, not that line. This block is not installed;
     bin/deploy-launchd-render.sh drops it. -->
<!-- docs/reference/checks.md `findings` (harbor#856): once a day, reconcile the lint census into the finding
     issues, then run the HEAL-lane repairs. Approved by the operator on 2026-10-02: daily,
     reconcile and heal, as the operator's own `gh` login, from main fetched off GitHub.

     It runs the INSTALLED lint-findings-run.sh, never the checkout (see its header), and that copy
     clones main fresh from a pinned URL, with system and global git config off, and runs that
     clone's own lint-findings.sh.
     Heal opens draft PRs at most; nothing merges without the operator.

     TEMPLATE: launchd does not expand $HOME, so replace @HOME@ with your home dir on
     install. An agent cannot install this, by design. Operator steps, in order:

       sh ~/port/harbor/bin/deploy-runtime-install.sh --live --apply
       # then install this plist into ~/Library/LaunchAgents and bootstrap it under gui/$(id -u)

     See it work: `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.harbor.findings`, then
     `jq . ~/.claude/cache/findings-state.json` and `cat /tmp/com.harbor.findings.out`.

     IT NEEDS THE KEYCHAIN for `gh`'s token, hence Aqua. DAILY AT 09:23: a full lint run is about
     70 seconds, and an off-minute keeps it clear of the jobs at 08:47 and 09:00.

     Disable (docs/reference/checks.md's two-lookup rule):
       launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.harbor.findings
       rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.harbor.findings.plist -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.harbor.findings</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/sh</string>
    <string>@HOME@/.claude/bin/lint-findings-run.sh</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key><integer>9</integer>
    <key>Minute</key><integer>23</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
  <key>LimitLoadToSessionType</key><string>Aqua</string>
  <key>ProcessType</key><string>Background</string>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <!-- System dirs first, and no ~/.local/bin: a session can Write a `git` there, and this job
         runs it unfenced. /opt/homebrew/bin stays, last, for gh, jq and shellcheck; it is
         operator-owned by design, and that box-wide exposure is harbor#902's. -->
    <key>PATH</key><string>/usr/bin:/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin</string>
    <key>HOME</key><string>@HOME@</string>
  </dict>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/tmp/com.harbor.findings.out</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/tmp/com.harbor.findings.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
